    #      spec's copy check, and the copy built from S byte for byte),
    #      rels_set (ruling 1), comments_same and notes_placed (the spec's
    #      carried checks), workbook_sheet, types_set, chain_rule, rest_same,
    #      xml_values and flagged (P2's). The lines' relations are the spec's:
    #      one sheet more, the copy's counts its source's, no chain after a
    #      formula. The tool's counts equal the comparison's.
    #  XD. NEW, the survey (copysurvey.py, <scripts>, copied into <work> and
    #      printed) replaces VD's, in its form: <corpus> its parameter, every
    #      regular file of <corpus>/corpus listed, one wb line of twenty fields
    #      per workbook; the log checks its forms, prints the distributions and
    #      checks every line's figures against it, and the comparison's parts
    #      against it. No drawings line (no decision rests on one here).
    #  XE. Changes PE, QE, SE and VE (every row ok) stand. The entries rule is
    #      the rulings during P3's: the copy's entry added; its rels part added
    #      exactly when S has a hyperlink or a comments relationship (ruling 1);
    #      the comments and VML parts added when carried; the workbook part, its
    #      rels part and the content types changed, flagged descriptor at most;
    #      the chain's entry dropped exactly when S holds a formula and the
    #      workbook a chain; every other row identical and unflagged; nothing
    #      recompressed. Each allowance has a control that accepts it where it
    #      applies and one that refuses it where it does not. The summary's
    #      totals are checked against what the rows imply and against the
    #      entries table.
    #  XF. NEW, the three earlier samples once more on both targets, their
    #      outputs by sha256, their lines and their diff tables P2's runs' byte
    #      for byte (change VF's form for three samples), the run directories
    #      read from the "the run directories:" line of P2's run log at P2's
    #      record commit and checked against the run directory P2's committed
    #      anchor record names; no record pair is written for the reruns.
    #  XG. Change UG's no-row rule gives way: the copy makes the write a formula
    #      change when S holds a formula (specs/0013's rule, "The copy"), so
    #      each chain workbook's calcChain row is dropped exactly there, and is
    #      identical and unflagged elsewhere; some row is dropped.
    #  XH. Change PH (the open check's own TMPDIR device) stands, unchanged.
    #  XI. The plants: every flag's planted control runs on the first ok
    #      workbook in manifest order of the plain case (S's comments not
    #      carried) and of the carried case, each on its own check line, the
    #      plant turning its own flag; every flag has a plant on both cases.
    #      The xml values check wants some value written (the workbook's new
    #      sheet; change LF's form).
    #  XJ. The run loop, the record pair, the keep and the open check are VJ's
    #      with this phase's names; the record's families are derived from its
    #      entries table, which the rule checked row by row; four record files
    #      installed, two when the keep is skipped.
    #  XK. Ruling 8 of the planning rulings during P2 (build pruning) and
    #      ruling 10 of the planning rulings during P3 (one target root per
    #      phase, one subdirectory per source tree): the phase's target root is
    #      <target>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/target, and every build
    #      of <repo> by this script, dry or logged, goes into <target>/main
    #      (CARGO_TARGET_DIR), the subdirectory ruling 10 gives the main tree;
    #      this script builds from no other tree. P2's <build> placeholder (a
    #      run directory holding its own target) is gone with the input
    #      RUN_BUILD_ROOT, so no run moves the builds, and nothing here cleans
    #      them; the i686 keep is <work>/keep-i686, kept, not under the target.
    #      VK stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`.
    #
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 6 P4 from M3 part 6 P3's run script (at the phase
    # commit 6a90674, printed in records/logs/m3p6-p3/run.log; its change lists
    # up to XK are above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p4/gen/
    # run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as often as it says, the top
    # summary replaced, the build section replaced by the size log's binaries,
    # the copy sample's record pair carried into the earlier samples' loop by
    # its anchor lines, and the body grepped afterwards for P3's names,
    # subjects and tokens. copycmp.py and copysurvey.py are P3's, copied beside
    # this script byte for byte. What differs, and why:
    #  YA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p4/scripts, on the disk)
    #      and the keep (m3p6-p4/keep-host) are this phase's; the base is P3's
    #      record commit ("M3 part 6 P3 record:"); the phase commit is P4's
    #      catalogue and probes commit by its subject ("M3 part 6 P4: the
    #      catalogue and limits, the probes"); the four samples each have a run
    #      directory <runs>/<date>-<sha>-<sample> and a record stem
    #      m3p6-p4-<sample>-<date>-<sha> (the spec's names, "P4"); SAMPLES is
    #      still the copy sample, whose checks are P3's, and RERUNS the three
    #      earlier samples; SUPERSEDED_RUN names the four by their common stem;
    #      the spec pinned through SPEC_SHA at P4's doc commit, planning's
    #      rulings during P4 standing uncommitted in the working tree's copy,
    #      printed. The usage takes the size.log as its third argument.
    #  YB. Change XB's form: the committed open-check record the keep is
    #      compared with is P3's, the last committed, named by its record
    #      commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 6 P3 record:"; no hash is
    #      typed here); it is the base itself, the parent of P4's doc commit; the
    #      control names the doc commit instead. P3_REC names the same commit,
    #      the one whose run directories the four samples are compared with
    #      (change YF).
    #  YC. Part 5 P3's change RC: the release binaries are the size log's, run
    #      where it built them (<target>/main/release and
    #      <target>/main/i686-unknown-linux-musl/release, the main tree's subdirectory, ruling 10
    #      of the planning rulings during P3), each hashed here and compared with
    #      its "hash: <name> <target> <sha256>" line in the size.log given, none
    #      built here; the size.log checked to be this phase's at this phase
    #      commit and to end all as expected. The run row's binaries are checked
    #      against the same hashes as before.
    #  YD. The survey (change XD) and the comparison (change XC) are P3's, byte
    #      for byte, run over the copy sample as P3's run did.
    #  YE. The earlier samples' rows: every row ok, every input and output
    #      opening in LibreOffice with no leftover, and the summary's status
    #      totals the entries table's; their entry rules are P2's and P1's, and
    #      hold here because every diff table is P3's run's byte for byte
    #      (change YF), whose run log checked them against P2's runs, which
    #      checked the rules.
    #  YF. Change XF's form for four samples: every sample, the copy sample
    #      included, compared on both targets with P3's run directory for it,
    #      its outputs by sha256, its lines and its diff tables byte for byte,
    #      every workbook's outcome and exit equal; the run directories read
    #      from the "the run directories:" line of P3's run log at P3's record
    #      commit and checked against the run directory P3's committed copy
    #      record names.
    #  YJ. Change XJ's record pair for each of the four samples: the copy
    #      sample's as P3's, and the three earlier samples' through the same
    #      record script and record check, their families derived from their
    #      entries tables; ten record files installed, eight when the keep is
    #      skipped.
    #  YK. Ruling 8 of the planning rulings during P2 and ruling 10 of those
    #      during P3: the phase's target root is <target>, <home>/.cache/
    #      emend-build/m3p6-p4/target; the keep's tests build into <target>/main
    #      (CARGO_TARGET_DIR), where size.log built the release binaries this
    #      log runs; nothing here cleans it. VK stands: this script runs no
    #      `rm -rf`.
    #
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 7 P3 from M3 part 6 P4's run script (at the phase
    # commit 9cfd92e, printed in records/logs/m3p6-p4/run.log; its change lists
    # up to YK are above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p3/gen/
    # run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as often as it says, the top
    # summary replaced, the keep and open-check sections removed, and the body
    # grepped afterwards for part 6 P4's names, subjects and tokens.
    # copycmp.py and copysurvey.py are part 6 P4's, copied beside this script
    # byte for byte. What differs, and why:
    #  RNA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the script directory
    #       (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p3/scripts, on the disk)
    #       are this phase's; the base is part 7 P2's record commit ("M3 part 7
    #       P2 record:"); the phase commit is P3's code commit by its subject
    #       ("M3 part 7 P3: rust-version equal to the pin, and the gate checks
    #       the pins agree"); the four samples each have a run directory
    #       <runs>/<date>-<sha>-<sample> and a record stem
    #       m3p7-p3-<sample>-<date>-<sha> (specs/0029 "Harness runs"); the spec
    #       is specs/0029, pinned through SPEC_SHA at this phase's doc commit. The usage
    #       takes the size.log as its second argument, and no test.log.
    #  RNB. The run directories the four samples are compared with are part 6
    #       P4's, named by its record commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 6
    #       P4 record:"; no hash is typed here), an ancestor of the phase commit,
    #       read from the "the run directories:" line of part 6 P4's run log at
    #       that commit and checked against the run directory its committed copy
    #       record names.
    #  RNC. The keep and the open check go, with their inputs (RUN_KEEP,
    #       RUN_SKIP_KEEP, SUPERSEDED_KEEP), the test.log argument, the <keep>
    #       root and the open record's stem: specs/0029 "Harness runs" names the
    #       four samples alone. The record files installed are the four pairs,
    #       eight.
    #  RND. Each sample's record header names its binaries (specs/0029 item 5):
    #       the .md holds one "- Binaries (host)" and one "- Binaries (i686)"
    #       line whose two hashes are the binaries this log ran, with a control.
    #  RNE. The size.log is this phase's (its "about:" line names P3's phase
    #       commit).
    #  RNF. The phase's target root is <target>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/
    #       m3p7-p3/target (specs/0001 "Rules for every phase", one target root
    #       per phase); this log builds nothing and runs the release binaries
    #       size.log built in <target>/main.
    #  RNG. The runner gives each child its own TMPDIR under its own work
    #       directory, under <work>/tmp-run here (specs/0029 P1 ruling 2); the
    #       check that <work>/tmp-run is empty after each run stands.
    #
    # Usage: [DRY=yes] m3p7-p5-run.sh <phase commit> > <file outside the tree>;
    # the caller moves the output to records/logs/m3p7-p5/run.log.
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$SELF_DIR/out/run.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    DRY=${DRY:-no}
    case $DRY in yes | no) ;; *) echo "DRY is yes or no" >&2; exit 2 ;; esac
    CORPUS_SET=$([ -n "${EMEND_CORPUS_DIR:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset)
    KEEP_SET=$([ -n "${EMEND_KEEP_DIR:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset)
    CORPUS=$HOME/emend-testing
    unset EMEND_CORPUS_DIR EMEND_KEEP_DIR
    export RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    PHASE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p5
    TARGET_ROOT=$PHASE_DIR/target
    export CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TARGET_ROOT/main
    BUILD_ROOT=$PHASE_DIR/run
    SUPERSEDED_DIR=$PHASE_DIR/superseded
    IMAGE=localhost/emend-lo:25.2.3-2-deb13u6
    LO_TIMEOUT_S=600
    SPEC=specs/0029-engineering-close.md
    SPEC_WANT=dad50b9c5f8b8b3f1a5ab43f0372c76fa346f563e1f95caf68de0cbb5451ad79
    P4_CHECKER=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p4/scripts/readme_check.py
    P4_RUNLOG=records/logs/m3p7-p4/run.log
    DATE=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)
    SHORT=${C:0:7}
    if [ "$DRY" = yes ]; then
      PREFIX=dry-
      KEEP=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m3p1-p3/keep-host
      DRY_RECORD=records/m3p1-open-2026-10-02-6578925.txt
      STAGE=$CORPUS/work/dry-excel-check-m2-$DATE
    else
      PREFIX=
      KEEP=$PHASE_DIR/keep-host
      DRY_RECORD=
      STAGE=$CORPUS/work/excel-check-m2-$DATE
    fi
    ZIP=$STAGE.zip
    STEM_OPEN=m3p7-open-$DATE-$SHORT
    mkdir -p "$BUILD_ROOT" || exit 2
    B=$(mktemp -d -p "$BUILD_ROOT") || exit 2
    git show "$C:scripts/counting.sh" >"$B/counting.sh" || exit 2
    . "$B/counting.sh"
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    fail=0
    check() { echo "  $1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || fail=1; }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    # For a condition that must NOT hold: a leading bang inside yn runs a
    # command named by the bang (specs/0001), so a negation has its own helper.
    ynnot() { if "$@"; then echo no; else echo yes; fi; }
    sha_of() { sha256sum <"$1" | cut -d' ' -f1; }
    
    head_is() { [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$1" ]; }
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    # The given commit is the phase commit when it is a full sha and HEAD.
    given_ok() { full_sha "$1" && head_is "$1"; }
    if given_ok "$C"; then :; else echo "the phase commit must be a full 40-hex sha that is HEAD, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    case "${C: -1}" in 0) LAST=1 ;; *) LAST=0 ;; esac
    FAKE_SHA=${C:0:39}$LAST
    # This phase's log directory, planning's working spec and the phase's record
    # files (change XLI).
    OURS="^((\\?\\?| ?[MARCD]) records/logs/m3p7-p5/| M specs/0029-engineering-close[.]md\$|\\?\\? records/m3p7-(p5-[a-z-]+|open)-$DATE-$SHORT[.](md|txt)\$)"
    entry_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    entry_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    entry_clean() { [ "$entry_all" != error ] && [ "$entry_ours" != error ] && [ "$entry_all" = "$entry_ours" ]; }
    if entry_clean; then :; else
      echo "the working tree holds changes outside this phase's logs, records and planning's spec" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    # The keep and the stage are this run's to make (changes XLE, XLF).
    if [ "$DRY" = no ] && [ -e "$KEEP" ]; then echo "the keep is already there; this run makes it" >&2; exit 2; fi
    for p in "$STAGE" "$ZIP"; do
      if [ -e "$p" ]; then echo "the stage or its zip is already there; this run makes them" >&2; exit 2; fi
    done
    
    scrub() {
      sed -e "s#$MAIN#<repo>#g" -e "s#$SELF_DIR#<scripts>#g" -e "s#$B#<work>#g" \
        -e "s#$BUILD_ROOT#<build>#g" -e "s#$SUPERSEDED_DIR#<superseded>#g" \
        -e "s#$TARGET_ROOT#<target>#g" -e "s#$CORPUS/runs#<runs>#g" -e "s#$CORPUS#<corpus>#g" \
        -e "s#$KEEP#<keep>#g" -e "s#$PHASE_DIR#<phase>#g" -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"
    }
    exec 3>&1
    exec > >(scrub >&3)
    SCRUB_PID=$!
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "invocation: bash <scripts>/$(basename "$0") $*"
    # The environment and path inputs, each on its labelled line.
    echo "input: DRY: $DRY"
    echo "input: RERUN_NOTE: ${RERUN_NOTE:-unset}"
    echo "input: RERUN_FILES: ${RERUN_FILES:-unset}"
    echo "input: EMEND_CORPUS_DIR: $CORPUS_SET (unset for the whole log); EMEND_KEEP_DIR: $KEEP_SET (unset for the whole log, set only on the keep's cargo test)"
    echo "input: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset) (its value never printed)"
    echo "input: HOME: set, read for the paths under it, printed as <home>"
    echo "about: M3 part 7 P5 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps, over this script, before its log (specs/0001)"
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" >"$B/shape-fixture"
    echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape"
    for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN; do
      var=SHAPE_$shape
      n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SELF")
      n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$B/shape-fixture")
      echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
      check "$shape: this script holds none" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
      check "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 1 ])"
    done
    check "control: ynnot reports no on a passing command" "$(yn [ "$(ynnot true)" = no ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role, read from git"
    by_subject() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1"; }
    REC=$(by_subject 'M3 part 7 P4 record: logs, the independent check')
    DOC1=$(by_subject 'M3 part 7 P5: commit planning docs (the P4 rulings and verification, the P5 phase)')
    CODE1=$(by_subject "M3 part 7 P5: the README's two sentences")
    echo "command: git log --format=%H -n 1 -F --grep=<the role's subject>, for each role"
    echo "  M3 part 7 P4's record commit (the base): ${REC:-none}"
    echo "  the doc commit: ${DOC1:-none}"
    echo "  the code commit (the README's two sentences, the phase commit): ${CODE1:-none}"
    echo "command: git rev-parse <phase commit>~0 to <phase commit>~2"
    for k in 0 1 2; do git rev-parse "$C~$k"; done | sed 's/^/    /'
    roles_in_order() {
      local r k=0
      for r in "$CODE1" "$DOC1" "$REC"; do
        [ -n "$r" ] || return 1
        [ "$(git rev-parse "$C~$k")" = "$r" ] || return 1
        k=$((k + 1))
      done
    }
    check "the code commit, the doc commit and the base, each the next one's parent, the code commit the phase commit (change XLA)" "$(yn roles_in_order)"
    roles_ctl() { local CODE1=$DOC1; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the code commit" "$(ynnot roles_ctl)"
    echo
    echo "phase: Milestone 3 part 7 P5 ($SPEC) run.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "rerun: the superseded files are kept in <superseded>"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")"
        else
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time\n' "$(basename "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"; fi
    fi
    n_cargo=$(pgrep -x cargo | wc -l)
    n_rustc=$(pgrep -x rustc | wc -l)
    echo "SERIALIZED: no other log run was in flight; cargo processes at entry: $n_cargo; rustc processes at entry: $n_rustc"
    no_build_running() { [ "$((n_cargo + n_rustc))" = 0 ]; }
    check "no cargo or rustc process was running at entry" "$(yn no_build_running)"
    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level (inside <home>, so scrubbed first); scripts/passthrough-run.sh, scripts/passthrough-record.py and scripts/edit-open-check.sh are run from it (the runner and the open check each source scripts/lo-check.sh); scripts/counting.sh, scripts/excel-check-list.py, scripts/excel-check-open.ps1, README.md and the records read are taken from it by git show at the phase commit; the record pairs are installed into its records/ (not in a dry run)"
    echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
    echo "root: <scripts> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p5/scripts, this script's own directory on the disk, which holds the script and, in <scripts>/out, its own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    echo "root: <phase> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p5, the phase's directory on the disk"
    echo "root: <target> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p5/target, the phase's one target root (specs/0001); <target>/main is the main tree's, where R0 builds the release binaries and R3 runs the keep's tests"
    echo "root: <build> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p5/run, the build root on the disk; nothing is built there"
    echo "root: <work> stands for this run's mktemp -d working directory under <build>, kept on the disk after the run: the library, the copies read at the phase commit, the runs' TMPDIR (<work>/tmp-run), the open check's TMPDIR (<work>/tmp), the record pairs before they are installed (<work>/records) and the controls' files"
    echo "root: <superseded> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p5/superseded, where a rerun's superseded files are kept; read only"
    echo "root: <corpus> stands for the private corpus directory; its manifest.tsv and corpus/ are read by the runner, never printed; the list's stage is made under <corpus>/work"
    echo "root: <runs> stands for <corpus>/runs, the corpus run directories: the reruns are written there, and every directory's run.host.tsv and summary.host.tsv are read for flags, start times and outcome counts"
    echo "root: <keep> stands for $([ "$DRY" = yes ] && echo "<home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p1-p3/keep-host, M3 part 1 P3's host keep, read only (the dry run)" || echo "<home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p5/keep-host, the host keep this run makes (R3)")"
    echo "root: <dir> stands for one directory under <runs>, each in turn, in the survey's command line"
    echo "root: <source> stands for a list row's source column (corpus, fixture or input) in the stage's layout files/<source>/<file> (specs/0016 P1 ruling 4), <file> the row's file column; the stage is under <corpus>/work"
    echo "root: <scratch> stands for a directory of an earlier phase's log and appears in this log only in the printed script's carried history; this log reads and writes nothing under it (change XLA)"
    apart() { case "$1/" in "$2"/*) return 1 ;; esac; case "$2/" in "$1"/*) return 1 ;; esac; return 0; }
    roots_distinct() { apart "$BUILD_ROOT" "$MAIN" && apart "$BUILD_ROOT" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$MAIN" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$TARGET_ROOT" "$BUILD_ROOT" && apart "$CORPUS" "$MAIN" && apart "$CORPUS" "$PHASE_DIR"; }
    check "the roots are distinct, none inside another (<work> inside <build>, <build>, <target> and <scripts> inside <phase>)" "$(yn roots_distinct)"
    roots_ctl() { apart "$B" "$BUILD_ROOT"; }
    check "control: apart refuses <work> against <build>, which holds it" "$(ynnot roots_ctl)"
    echo "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set in this shell: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    key_unset() { [ -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ]; }
    check "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set" "$(yn key_unset)"
    key_set_ctl() { local ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=planted; key_unset; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a shell where the variable is set" "$(ynnot key_set_ctl)"
    echo "at entry: status lines $entry_all; of them this phase's logs, records or planning's spec $entry_ours; the lines:"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo "  the controls' commits: the null commit $NULL_SHA; the fabricated commit $FAKE_SHA (the given one, its last hex digit changed); the short sha $SHORT"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(yn full_sha "$C")"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(yn head_is "$C")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the null commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$NULL_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a fabricated commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$FAKE_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a short sha of the real commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$SHORT")"
    short_names_head() { [ "$(git rev-parse "$SHORT")" = "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" ]; }
    check "control: the short sha is the real commit's, so only its form is refused" "$(yn short_names_head)"
    ours_ctl() { printf ' M scripts/check.sh\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified gate file" "$(ynnot ours_ctl)"
    ours_readme_ctl() { printf ' M README.md\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified README.md" "$(ynnot ours_readme_ctl)"
    ours_rec_ctl() { printf '?? records/logs/m3p7-p5/run.log\n?? records/logs/m3p7-p4/run.log\n?? records/m3p7-p5-edit-%s-%s.md\n?? records/m3p7-open-%s-%s.txt\n?? records/m3p7-p5-edit-2026-01-01-abcdef0.md\n M ROADMAP.md\n M specs/0029-engineering-close.md\n' "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" | count_matches -E "$OURS" /dev/stdin; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern takes this phase's log, its two record stems and planning's spec alone, no other phase's log, no record of another stem and no other planning file (change XLI)" "$(yn [ "$(ours_rec_ctl)" = 4 ])"
    SPEC_HAVE=$(sha256sum <"$SPEC" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    SPEC_BLOB=$(git show "$C:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$SPEC | sha256sum: $SPEC_BLOB; sha256sum $SPEC (the working file, printed and not asserted: planning holds its rulings during P5 uncommitted; change XLA): $SPEC_HAVE"
    check "the spec's blob at the phase commit is at the hash this log pins" "$(yn [ "$SPEC_BLOB" = "$SPEC_WANT" ])"
    spec_ctl() { [ "$(printf 'x' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$SPEC_WANT" ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the hash of another file" "$(ynnot spec_ctl)"
    echo
    echo "## script that wrote this log"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$SELF"
    echo
    echo "## the shared counting library this log sources"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/counting.sh"
    echo
    echo "## counting controls"
    counting_controls
    if [ "$counting_controls_ok" != yes ]; then fail=1; fi
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # The sample table (change XLD), in spec order from specs/0011 to specs/0028:
    # spec, flag (the tool argument is --<flag>-sample), name (the directory's
    # and the record's), and what this run does: rerun (its directories are gone,
    # or P4 ruling 2 reruns it) or found (its newest directory, expected below).
    SAMPLES="
    0011 edit edit rerun -
    0011 edit-formula edit-formula rerun -
    0012 style style rerun -
    0012 date date rerun -
    0013 formula formula rerun -
    0016 sheet sheet rerun -
    0016 remove remove rerun -
    0017 font font rerun -
    0017 border border rerun -
    0018 format format rerun -
    0018 insert-rows insert-rows rerun -
    0018 delete-rows delete-rows rerun -
    0018 insert-columns insert-columns rerun -
    0018 delete-columns delete-columns rerun -
    0019 names names rerun -
    0019 link link rerun -
    0019 props props rerun -
    0019 protect protect rerun -
    0020 validate validate rerun -
    0020 cf cf rerun -
    0020 scale scale rerun -
    0021 table table rerun -
    0022 comment comment found 2026-10-02-6578925-comment
    0022 image image found 2026-10-02-6578925
    0024 richtext richtext found 2026-10-03-0c3e4fa-richtext
    0024 richcomment richcomment found 2026-10-03-0c3e4fa
    0025 sheetview sheetview found 2026-10-03-01b14c0-c-sheetview
    0025 pagesetup pagesetup found 2026-10-03-01b14c0-c-pagesetup
    0025 printarea printarea rerun -
    0026 group group found 2026-10-05-ef392d4-group
    0026 linestyle linestyle found 2026-10-05-ef392d4-linestyle
    0027 read read found 2026-10-05-6b6125b-read
    0027 roundtrip roundtrip found 2026-10-05-6b6125b-roundtrip
    0028 anchor anchor found 2026-10-09-09d2e0f-anchor
    0028 commentbox commentbox found 2026-10-09-09d2e0f-commentbox
    0028 copy copy found 2026-10-09-09d2e0f-copy
    0028 remove-image removeimage found 2026-10-09-09d2e0f-removeimage
    "
    printf '%s\n' "$SAMPLES" | awk 'NF == 5' >"$B/samples.tbl"
    n_samples=$(count_lines "$B/samples.tbl")
    n_rerun_tbl=$(awk '$4 == "rerun"' "$B/samples.tbl" | wc -l)
    n_found_tbl=$(awk '$4 == "found"' "$B/samples.tbl" | wc -l)
    # Outcome counts of a summary, by the outcome column found by its header
    # name: "ok 27" and so on, one pair per outcome, sorted.
    outcome_counts() { awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "outcome") o = i; next } o { n[$o]++ } END { for (k in n) print k, n[k] }' "$1" | LC_ALL=C sort | tr '\n' ' '; }
    # Rows of a summary whose outcome is not ok.
    not_ok_rows() { awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "outcome") o = i; next } o && $o != "ok" { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    printf 'id\tlabel\toutcome\nw1\thost\tok\nw2\thost\terror\nw3\thost\tok\n' >"$B/c-summary.tsv"
    check "control: outcome_counts reads a fixture by its header (error 1, ok 2)" "$(yn [ "$(outcome_counts "$B/c-summary.tsv")" = "error 1 ok 2 " ])"
    check "control: not_ok_rows counts the fixture's one error row" "$(yn [ "$(not_ok_rows "$B/c-summary.tsv")" = 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the sample table: specs, flags and what this run does (changes XLD; Planning rulings during P5 (2026-10-09), ruling 1)"
    echo "  spec, flag, name, rerun or found, the directory the facts expect when found:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/samples.tbl"
    echo "  samples $n_samples; rerun $n_rerun_tbl; found $n_found_tbl"
    check "every row of the table is rerun or found" "$(yn [ "$n_samples" = "$((n_rerun_tbl + n_found_tbl))" ])"
    spec_order() { [ "$(cut -d' ' -f1 "$B/samples.tbl" | tr '\n' ' ')" = "$(cut -d' ' -f1 "$B/samples.tbl" | LC_ALL=C sort -s | tr '\n' ' ')" ]; }
    check "the table is in spec order, specs/0011 to specs/0028" "$(yn spec_order)"
    git ls-tree -r --name-only "$C" -- tools/emend-copy/src | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '[.]rs$' >"$B/tool.files"
    : >"$B/tool.src"
    while IFS= read -r f; do git show "$C:$f" >>"$B/tool.src"; done <"$B/tool.files"
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:<each .rs file under tools/emend-copy/src> ($(count_lines "$B/tool.files") files); for each flag, grep -c -F '\"--<flag>-sample\"'"
    n_flags_there=0
    while read -r spec flag name mode want; do
      n=$(count_matches -F "\"--$flag-sample\"" "$B/tool.src")
      [ "$n" -ge 1 ] && n_flags_there=$((n_flags_there + 1))
      echo "    --$flag-sample: $n"
    done <"$B/samples.tbl"
    check "every flag of the table is in the tool's source at the phase commit" "$(yn [ "$n_flags_there" = "$n_samples" ])"
    check "control: the same count finds no such flag as --no-such-sample" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -F '"--no-such-sample"' "$B/tool.src")" = 0 ])"
    new_out() { [ "$(awk '$2 == "new"' "$B/samples.tbl" | wc -l)" = 0 ]; }
    check "the table holds no new sample (specs/0016: the runner does not run it over the corpus)" "$(yn new_out)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the run directories on the disk, surveyed before any run (change XLD)"
    # One line per directory under <runs> with a run.host.tsv: the flag in its
    # tool_args column (the first row's), its started time, its name; a
    # directory whose tool_args is empty is listed as such and never taken.
    survey() {
      local d
      for d in "$CORPUS"/runs/*/; do
        d=${d%/}
        [ -f "$d/run.host.tsv" ] || continue
        awk -F'\t' -v n="$(basename "$d")" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) { if ($i == "tool_args") t = i; if ($i == "started") s = i } next } NR == 2 { a = (t ? $t : ""); sub(/^--/, "", a); sub(/-sample$/, "", a); if (a == "") a = "-"; print a "\t" (s ? $s : "-") "\t" n }' "$d/run.host.tsv"
      done
    }
    survey >"$B/survey.tsv"
    echo "command: for each <runs>/<dir>/run.host.tsv, awk by header name for tool_args and started (the first row); the flag is tool_args less its -- and -sample"
    echo "  directories with a run.host.tsv: $(count_lines "$B/survey.tsv"); of them with an empty tool_args: $(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "-"' "$B/survey.tsv" | wc -l)"
    awk -F'\t' '{ print "    " $3 "\t" $1 "\t" $2 }' "$B/survey.tsv"
    printf 'a\tb\tstarted\tc\ttool_args\n1\t2\t2026-01-02T00:00:00Z\t3\t--x-y-sample\n' >"$B/c-run.tsv"
    survey_ctl() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' -v n=d 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) { if ($i == "tool_args") t = i; if ($i == "started") s = i } next } NR == 2 { a = (t ? $t : ""); sub(/^--/, "", a); sub(/-sample$/, "", a); print a "\t" $s "\t" n }' "$B/c-run.tsv")" = "x-y${TAB}2026-01-02T00:00:00Z${TAB}d" ]; }
    check "control: the survey's form reads a fixture's columns by name, the flag with a hyphen inside" "$(yn survey_ctl)"
    # newest <flag>: the directory whose run.host.tsv names the flag, latest
    # started, from the survey taken before any run.
    newest() { awk -F'\t' -v f="$1" '$1 == f' "$B/survey.tsv" | LC_ALL=C sort -t "$TAB" -k2,2 | tail -n 1 | cut -f3; }
    dirs_of() { awk -F'\t' -v f="$1" '$1 == f' "$B/survey.tsv" | wc -l; }
    printf 'f\t2026-01-01T00:00:01Z\tz-old\nf\t2026-01-01T00:00:09Z\ta-new\n' >"$B/c-survey.tsv"
    newest_ctl() { [ "$(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "f"' "$B/c-survey.tsv" | LC_ALL=C sort -t "$TAB" -k2,2 | tail -n 1 | cut -f3)" = a-new ]; }
    check "control: newest takes the latest started time, not the last name (a-new over z-old)" "$(yn newest_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## TMPDIR for the corpus runs, on the disk (part 6 P4's change LG)"
    RUNTMP=$B/tmp-run
    mkdir "$RUNTMP" "$B/tmp" "$B/records" || exit 2
    dev_tmp=$(stat -c %d "$RUNTMP")
    dev_corpus=$(stat -c %d "$CORPUS/corpus")
    dev_proc=$(stat -c %d /proc)
    echo "command: mkdir <work>/tmp-run <work>/tmp <work>/records; stat -c %d <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus /proc"
    echo "  device of TMPDIR (<work>/tmp-run): $dev_tmp; of the corpus directory (<corpus>/corpus): $dev_corpus; of /proc (the control): $dev_proc"
    check "TMPDIR for the corpus runs and the corpus directory are on one device" "$(yn [ "$dev_tmp" = "$dev_corpus" ])"
    dev_ctl() { if [ "$dev_proc" = "$dev_corpus" ]; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same comparison tells /proc's device from the corpus directory's" "$(yn dev_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## R0. the release binaries, built in <target>/main at the phase commit (change XLC)"
    echo "command: cargo build --release -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff --offline (CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main)"
    cargo build --release -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff --offline >"$B/build.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $rc"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^ *(Compiling|Finished) ' "$B/build.out" | sed 's/^ */    /'
    check "the release build exits 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" = 0 ])"
    PT=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/emend-copy
    XD=$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/xlsx-diff
    bins_there() { [ -x "$PT" ] && [ -x "$XD" ]; }
    check "both release binaries are there and executable" "$(yn bins_there)"
    echo "  hash: emend-copy host $(sha_of "$PT"), bytes $(stat -c %s "$PT")"
    echo "  hash: xlsx-diff host $(sha_of "$XD"), bytes $(stat -c %s "$XD")"
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    echo "## R1. the samples rerun on the host, one run per flag (change XLD; P4 ruling 2; P5 ruling 1)"
    : >"$B/plain.dirs"
    FORMULA_DIR=
    DRY_RUN_DIRS=()
    n_rerun_done=0
    n_rerun_want=0
    while read -r spec flag name mode want; do
      [ "$mode" = rerun ] || continue
      echo
      echo "### specs/$spec --$flag-sample"
      nd=$(dirs_of "$flag")
      echo "  directories on the disk whose run.host.tsv names --$flag-sample, before this run: $nd"
      if [ "$flag" = printarea ]; then
        echo "  rerun: P4 ruling 2 reruns printarea; its directories' outcome counts:"
        awk -F'\t' -v f="$flag" '$1 == f { print $3 }' "$B/survey.tsv" | while IFS= read -r d; do echo "    $d: $(outcome_counts "$CORPUS/runs/$d/summary.host.tsv")"; done
      else
        check "specs/$spec --$flag-sample: its run directory is gone from <runs>, so it is rerun" "$(yn [ "$nd" = 0 ])"
      fi
      if [ "$DRY" = yes ] && [ "$flag" != formula ]; then
        echo "  the dry run reruns the formula sample alone: skipped, and left out of the dry list"
        continue
      fi
      n_rerun_want=$((n_rerun_want + 1))
      O=$CORPUS/runs/$PREFIX$DATE-$SHORT-$name
      STEM=m3p7-p5-$name-$DATE-$SHORT
      if [ -e "$O" ]; then
        check "specs/$spec --$flag-sample: the run directory <runs>/${O##*/} is not there before the run" "no"
        continue
      fi
      check "specs/$spec --$flag-sample: the run directory <runs>/${O##*/} is not there before the run" "yes"
      [ "$DRY" = yes ] && DRY_RUN_DIRS+=("$O")
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label host --passthrough <target>/main/release/emend-copy --xlsx-diff <target>/main/release/xlsx-diff --out <runs>/${O##*/} --libreoffice $IMAGE --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S --timeout 300 --tool-arg --$flag-sample"
      started=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
      TMPDIR=$RUNTMP scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label host --passthrough "$PT" --xlsx-diff "$XD" --out "$O" \
        --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --lo-timeout "$LO_TIMEOUT_S" --timeout 300 --tool-arg "--$flag-sample" \
        >"$B/run-$name.stdout" 2>"$B/run-$name.stderr" </dev/null
      rc=$?
      echo "  started $started; ended $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ); exit $rc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/run-$name.stderr")"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$B/run-$name.stdout"
      check "--$flag-sample: the run exits 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" = 0 ])"
      check "--$flag-sample: its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/run-$name.stderr" ])"
      n_left=$(find "$RUNTMP" -mindepth 1 | wc -l)
      echo "  entries left in <work>/tmp-run after the run: $n_left"
      check "--$flag-sample: the runs' TMPDIR is empty after the run" "$(yn [ "$n_left" = 0 ])"
      SUM=$O/summary.host.tsv
      rows=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$SUM" | wc -l)
      bad=$(not_ok_rows "$SUM")
      echo "  summary.host.tsv: rows $rows; outcomes: $(outcome_counts "$SUM"); rows not ok: $bad"
      check "--$flag-sample: the summary holds one row per manifest workbook ($(awk 'NR > 1' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv" | wc -l))" "$(yn [ "$rows" = "$(awk 'NR > 1' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv" | wc -l)" ])"
      if [ "$bad" != 0 ]; then echo "  FINDING: --$flag-sample has $bad rows not ok; nothing is rerun to make them pass; the directory is left out of the list"; fi
      echo "command: scripts/passthrough-record.py --run <runs>/${O##*/} --out <work>/records --stem $STEM --allow-single"
      scripts/passthrough-record.py --run "$O" --out "$B/records" --stem "$STEM" --allow-single >"$B/record-$name.out" 2>"$B/record-$name.err" </dev/null
      rrc=$?
      echo "  exit: $rrc; stdout:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$B/record-$name.out"
      echo "  stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/record-$name.err")"
      rec_ran() { [ "$rrc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$B/record-$name.err" ]; }
      check "--$flag-sample: the record script exits 0, its stderr empty" "$(yn rec_ran)"
      rec_header() {
        [ -f "$B/records/$STEM.txt" ] && [ "$(count_matches -xF "- Commit: $C" "$B/records/$STEM.md")" = 1 ] \
          && [ "$(count_matches -xF '- Targets: host' "$B/records/$STEM.md")" = 1 ] \
          && [ "$(count_matches -xF "- Tool arguments: --$flag-sample" "$B/records/$STEM.md")" = 1 ]
      }
      check "--$flag-sample: the record pair is there, its .md naming the phase commit, the host alone and the flag" "$(yn rec_header)"
      echo "  record: $STEM.md sha256 $(sha_of "$B/records/$STEM.md"); $STEM.txt sha256 $(sha_of "$B/records/$STEM.txt")"
      n_rerun_done=$((n_rerun_done + 1))
      if [ "$flag" = formula ]; then
        FORMULA_DIR=$O
      elif [ "$bad" = 0 ]; then
        printf '%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$spec" "$flag" "$O" >>"$B/plain.dirs"
      fi
    done <"$B/samples.tbl"
    echo
    echo "  reruns done $n_rerun_done of $n_rerun_want"
    check "every rerun this run makes was made and recorded" "$(yn [ "$n_rerun_done" = "$n_rerun_want" ])"
    check "the formula sample's directory, the list's --run, was made" "$(yn [ -n "$FORMULA_DIR" ])"
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    echo "## R2. the samples found on the disk, each its newest directory by run.host.tsv (change XLD)"
    n_found_ok=0
    while read -r spec flag name mode want; do
      [ "$mode" = found ] || continue
      got=$(newest "$flag")
      SUM=$CORPUS/runs/$got/summary.host.tsv
      echo "  specs/$spec --$flag-sample: directories naming it $(dirs_of "$flag"); the newest by started: ${got:-none}; the facts expect: $want"
      found_is() { [ -n "$got" ] && [ "$got" = "$want" ] && [ -f "$SUM" ]; }
      if found_is; then
        n_found_ok=$((n_found_ok + 1))
        bad=$(not_ok_rows "$SUM")
        echo "    outcomes: $(outcome_counts "$SUM"); rows not ok: $bad"
        if [ "$bad" = 0 ]; then
          printf '%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$spec" "$flag" "$CORPUS/runs/$got" >>"$B/plain.dirs"
        else
          echo "    FINDING: <runs>/$got has $bad rows not ok; left out of the list"
        fi
      fi
      check "specs/$spec --$flag-sample: found, the expected directory, with its host summary" "$(yn found_is)"
    done <"$B/samples.tbl"
    check "every sample the table finds was found" "$(yn [ "$n_found_ok" = "$n_found_tbl" ])"
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    if [ "$DRY" = yes ]; then
      echo "## R3. the keep and the open check: SKIPPED (DRY=yes; change XLH): the list takes <keep>, M3 part 1 P3's host keep, and $DRY_RECORD"
      git show "$C:$DRY_RECORD" >"$B/open.txt" || exit 2
      RECORD_TXT=$B/open.txt
      echo "  the record read at the phase commit: sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORD_TXT"), rows $(awk 'NR > 1' "$RECORD_TXT" | wc -l); files in <keep>: $(find "$KEEP" -type f | wc -l)"
    else
      echo "## R3. the host keep regenerated, and opened by scripts/edit-open-check.sh (change XLE)"
      mkdir "$KEEP" || exit 2
      echo "command: EMEND_KEEP_DIR=<keep> cargo test --workspace (host; CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main)"
      EMEND_KEEP_DIR=$KEEP cargo test --workspace >"$B/keep.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
      rc=$?
      echo "  exit: $rc"
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^test result: ' "$B/keep.out" | sed 's/^/    /'
      failed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^failed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/keep.out")
      passed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^passed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/keep.out")
      echo "  passed $passed; failed $failed"
      check "the tests with the keep set exit 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" = 0 ])"
      check "no test failed" "$(yn [ "$failed" = 0 ])"
      n_in=$(find "$KEEP" -maxdepth 1 -type f -name '*.in.xlsx' | wc -l)
      n_out=$(find "$KEEP" -maxdepth 1 -type f -name '*.out.xlsx' | wc -l)
      n_all=$(find "$KEEP" -mindepth 1 | wc -l)
      echo "  the keep: inputs $n_in; outputs $n_out; entries in all $n_all"
      pairs_only() { [ "$n_in" -gt 0 ] && [ "$n_in" = "$n_out" ] && [ "$n_all" = "$((n_in + n_out))" ]; }
      check "the keep holds pairs and nothing else" "$(yn pairs_only)"
      dev_open=$(stat -c %d "$B/tmp")
      echo "  device of the open check's TMPDIR (<work>/tmp): $dev_open; of the corpus directory: $dev_corpus"
      check "the open check's TMPDIR and the corpus directory are on one device" "$(yn [ "$dev_open" = "$dev_corpus" ])"
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp scripts/edit-open-check.sh --keep <keep> --libreoffice $IMAGE --out <work>/records --stem $STEM_OPEN"
      TMPDIR=$B/tmp scripts/edit-open-check.sh --keep "$KEEP" --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --out "$B/records" --stem "$STEM_OPEN" \
        >"$B/oc.stdout" 2>"$B/oc.stderr" </dev/null
      oc_rc=$?
      echo "  exit: $oc_rc; stdout lines $(count_lines "$B/oc.stdout"); stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/oc.stderr")"
      echo "  its totals line:"; LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^(totals|wrote) ' "$B/oc.stdout" | sed 's/^/    /'
      check "the open check exits 0 (no finding, no check errored)" "$(yn [ "$oc_rc" = 0 ])"
      check "its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/oc.stderr" ])"
      RECORD_TXT=$B/records/$STEM_OPEN.txt
      open_pair() { [ -f "$RECORD_TXT" ] && [ -f "$B/records/$STEM_OPEN.md" ] && [ "$(awk 'NR > 1' "$RECORD_TXT" | wc -l)" = "$n_in" ]; }
      check "the open record pair is there, its .txt one row per kept pair" "$(yn open_pair)"
      echo "  record: $STEM_OPEN.md sha256 $(sha_of "$B/records/$STEM_OPEN.md"); $STEM_OPEN.txt sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORD_TXT")"
      echo "  the open record's totals table:"
      sed -n '/^## Totals/,/^## [A-Z]/p' "$B/records/$STEM_OPEN.md" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^[|]' | sed 's/^/    /'
    fi
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    echo "## R4. the list and its stage (change XLF; specs/0016 P1 rulings 1 to 4)"
    git show "$C:scripts/excel-check-list.py" >"$B/excel-check-list.py" || exit 2
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:scripts/excel-check-list.py > <work>/excel-check-list.py: sha256 $(sha_of "$B/excel-check-list.py")"
    PLAIN_ARGS=()
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r spec flag d; do PLAIN_ARGS+=(--run-plain "$d"); done <"$B/plain.dirs"
    echo "  the directories, in spec order: --run <runs>/${FORMULA_DIR##*/} (formula), then $(count_lines "$B/plain.dirs") --run-plain:"
    awk -F'\t' '{ n = split($3, p, "/"); print "    specs/" $1 " --" $2 "-sample: <runs>/" p[n] }' "$B/plain.dirs"
    plain_order() { [ "$(cut -f1 "$B/plain.dirs" | tr '\n' ' ')" = "$(cut -f1 "$B/plain.dirs" | LC_ALL=C sort -s | tr '\n' ' ')" ]; }
    check "the --run-plain directories are in spec order" "$(yn plain_order)"
    LIST=$STAGE/excel-check-list.txt
    mkdir -m 700 "$STAGE" "$STAGE/files" || exit 2
    echo "command: (umask 077; python3 -I <work>/excel-check-list.py --run <runs>/${FORMULA_DIR##*/} --run-plain <each directory above> --keep <keep> --record <the open record's .txt> --out <corpus>/work/${STAGE##*/}/excel-check-list.txt)"
    (umask 077; python3 -I "$B/excel-check-list.py" --run "$FORMULA_DIR" "${PLAIN_ARGS[@]}" --keep "$KEEP" --record "$RECORD_TXT" --out "$LIST" >"$B/ls.stdout" 2>"$B/ls.stderr" </dev/null)
    ls_rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $ls_rc"
    echo "  stdout:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$B/ls.stdout"
    echo "  stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/ls.stderr")"
    check "the list script exits 0" "$(yn [ "$ls_rc" = 0 ])"
    check "its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/ls.stderr" ])"
    nrows_l=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$LIST" | wc -l)
    n_corpus_rows=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR > 1 && $1 == "corpus"' "$LIST" | wc -l)
    n_fixture_rows=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR > 1 && $1 == "fixture"' "$LIST" | wc -l)
    n_input_rows=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR > 1 && $1 == "input"' "$LIST" | wc -l)
    n_manifest=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv" | wc -l)
    n_dirs=$((1 + $(count_lines "$B/plain.dirs")))
    echo "  the list (never committed, no row printed): <corpus>/work/${STAGE##*/}/excel-check-list.txt, sha256 $(sha_of "$LIST"), $(wc -c <"$LIST") bytes, mode $(stat -c %a "$LIST")"
    echo "  rows by source: corpus $n_corpus_rows; fixture $n_fixture_rows; input $n_input_rows; total $nrows_l"
    check "the list is mode 600" "$(yn [ "$(stat -c %a "$LIST")" = 600 ])"
    check "the list's header is the thirteen columns" "$(yn [ "$(head -n 1 "$LIST")" = "$(printf 'source\tid_or_test\tlabel\tfile\tbytes\tsha256\tresult\tref1\texpect1\tref2\texpect2\tref3\texpect3')" ])"
    check "the rows are corpus, fixture and input rows alone" "$(yn [ "$nrows_l" = "$((n_corpus_rows + n_fixture_rows + n_input_rows))" ])"
    check "the corpus rows are the manifest's $n_manifest workbooks once per directory, $n_dirs directories" "$(yn [ "$n_corpus_rows" = "$((n_manifest * n_dirs))" ])"
    check "one input row per fixture row" "$(yn [ "$n_fixture_rows" = "$n_input_rows" ])"
    bad_cols=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR > 1 && (NF != 13 || $7 != "")' "$LIST" | wc -l)
    check "every row has thirteen columns and an empty result ($bad_cols rows otherwise)" "$(yn [ "$bad_cols" = 0 ])"
    echo
    echo "## the staged directory and its zip (specs/0016 P1 ruling 4)"
    echo "command: install the script beside the list; each listed file copied to <corpus>/work/${STAGE##*/}/files/<source>/<file> (umask 077): corpus rows from <corpus>/<file>, fixture and input rows from <keep>/<file>"
    (
      umask 077
      git show "$C:scripts/excel-check-open.ps1" >"$STAGE/excel-check-open.ps1" || exit 2
      tail -n +2 "$LIST" | while IFS="$TAB" read -r src _ _ file _; do
        case $src in corpus) from=$CORPUS/$file ;; *) from=$KEEP/$file ;; esac
        mkdir -p "$STAGE/files/$src/$(dirname "$file")" || exit 2
        cp "$from" "$STAGE/files/$src/$file" || exit 2
      done
    )
    echo "  exit: $?"
    (cd "$STAGE" && find . -type f -printf '%P\n' | LC_ALL=C sort) >"$B/stage.files"
    n_staged=$(count_lines "$B/stage.files")
    n_datafiles=$(count_matches -E '^files/' "$B/stage.files")
    echo "  files staged: $n_staged; under files/: $n_datafiles; list rows: $nrows_l"
    check "the stage holds the list, the script and one file per list row, nothing else" "$(yn [ "$n_staged" = "$((nrows_l + 2))" ])"
    staged_ps1() { [ "$(sha_of "$STAGE/excel-check-open.ps1")" = "$(git show "$C:scripts/excel-check-open.ps1" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" ]; }
    check "the staged script is the phase commit's scripts/excel-check-open.ps1 (sha256 $(sha_of "$STAGE/excel-check-open.ps1"))" "$(yn staged_ps1)"
    nstaged_ok=0
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r src id label file bytes sha _; do
      p=$STAGE/files/$src/$file
      if [ -f "$p" ] && [ "$(stat -c %s "$p")" = "$bytes" ] && [ "$(sha_of "$p")" = "$sha" ]; then nstaged_ok=$((nstaged_ok + 1)); else echo "    staged file differs: $src $id $label"; fi
    done < <(tail -n +2 "$LIST")
    echo "  list rows whose staged file at files/<source>/<file> has the row's bytes and sha256: $nstaged_ok of $nrows_l"
    check "every staged file is the one its list row names, by bytes and sha256" "$(yn [ "$nstaged_ok" = "$nrows_l" ])"
    open_modes() { [ "$(find "$STAGE" -type f ! -perm 600 | wc -l)" = 0 ] && [ "$(find "$STAGE" -type d ! -perm 700 | wc -l)" = 0 ]; }
    check "every staged file is mode 600 and every staged directory 700" "$(yn open_modes)"
    echo "command: python3 zipfile, deflated, every staged file under the folder name ${STAGE##*/}/, written to <corpus>/work/${ZIP##*/} (umask 077)"
    (umask 077; python3 -I - "$STAGE" "$ZIP" <<'PY'
    import os, sys, zipfile
    stage, out = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]
    top = os.path.basename(stage)
    with zipfile.ZipFile(out, "x", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:
        for folder, dirs, files in os.walk(stage):
            dirs.sort()
            for name in sorted(files):
                path = os.path.join(folder, name)
                z.write(path, top + "/" + os.path.relpath(path, stage))
    PY
    )
    echo "  exit: $?"
    echo "  the zip (never committed): <corpus>/work/${ZIP##*/}, sha256 $(sha_of "$ZIP"), $(stat -c %s "$ZIP") bytes, mode $(stat -c %a "$ZIP")"
    python3 -I - "$STAGE" "$ZIP" >"$B/zipcheck.out" <<'PY'
    import hashlib, os, sys, zipfile
    stage, out = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]
    top = os.path.basename(stage)
    z = zipfile.ZipFile(out)
    names = z.namelist()
    same = sum(1 for n in names if n.startswith(top + "/") and os.path.isfile(os.path.join(stage, n[len(top) + 1:]))
               and hashlib.sha256(z.read(n)).digest() == hashlib.sha256(open(os.path.join(stage, n[len(top) + 1:]), "rb").read()).digest())
    print("entries %d; entries whose bytes are the staged file's: %d; testzip: %s" % (len(names), same, z.testzip() or "ok"))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/zipcheck.out"
    zip_whole() { [ "$(cat "$B/zipcheck.out")" = "entries $n_staged; entries whose bytes are the staged file's: $n_staged; testzip: ok" ]; }
    check "the zip holds every staged file once, byte for byte, and tests clean" "$(yn zip_whole)"
    check "the zip is mode 600" "$(yn [ "$(stat -c %a "$ZIP")" = 600 ])"
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    echo "## R5. the README check repeated with P4's program (P4 verification ruling 2; change XLB)"
    cp "$P4_CHECKER" "$B/readme_check.py" || exit 2
    git show "$C:$P4_RUNLOG" >"$B/p4-run.log" || exit 2
    P4_SHA=$(sed -n 's/^command: sha256sum <scripts>\/readme_check.py: \([0-9a-f]\{64\}\)$/\1/p' "$B/p4-run.log")
    echo "command: sha256sum <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p4/scripts/readme_check.py: $(sha_of "$B/readme_check.py"); the hash P4's run log printed, read from $P4_RUNLOG at the phase commit by sed: ${P4_SHA:-none}"
    check "the program is P4's, by the hash P4's run log printed" "$(yn [ "$(sha_of "$B/readme_check.py")" = "$P4_SHA" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses another file's hash" "$(ynnot [ "$(sha_of "$B/counting.sh")" = "$P4_SHA" ])"
    git show "$C:README.md" >"$B/README.md"
    git ls-tree -r --name-only "$C" >"$B/tree.txt"
    echo "command: python3 -I <work>/readme_check.py <work>/README.md <work>/tree.txt (README.md and the tree listing read at the phase commit)"
    python3 -I "$B/readme_check.py" "$B/README.md" "$B/tree.txt" >"$B/rc.out" 2>"$B/rc.err"
    rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $rc; the summary: $(tail -n 1 "$B/rc.out")"
    summary_is() { tail -n 1 "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "^sentences [0-9]+ with-digit [0-9]+ cited [0-9]+ $2\$"; }
    rc_ok() { [ "$rc" = 0 ] && summary_is "$B/rc.out" 'uncited 0 missing 0' && [ ! -s "$B/rc.err" ]; }
    check "every sentence of the README holding a digit cites a records/ path the tree holds" "$(yn rc_ok)"
    cp "$B/README.md" "$B/README-planted.md"
    printf '\nA planted sentence holding the figure 7 and citing nothing.\n' >>"$B/README-planted.md"
    python3 -I "$B/readme_check.py" "$B/README-planted.md" "$B/tree.txt" >"$B/rcp.out" 2>&1
    rcp=$?
    echo "  control, a planted uncited sentence: exit $rcp; the summary: $(tail -n 1 "$B/rcp.out")"
    rcp_ok() { [ "$rcp" = 1 ] && summary_is "$B/rcp.out" 'uncited 1 missing 0'; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the planted sentence" "$(yn rcp_ok)"
    echo "command: git diff <doc commit> <phase commit> -- README.md, the changed lines"
    git diff "$DOC1" "$C" -- README.md >"$B/readme.diff"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^[-+][^-+]' "$B/readme.diff" | sed 's/^/    /'
    n_minus=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -cE '^-[^-]' "$B/readme.diff")
    n_plus=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -cE '^[+][^+]' "$B/readme.diff")
    echo "  lines removed $n_minus; lines added $n_plus"
    check "the phase commit changes two lines of README.md, two removed and two added" "$(yn [ "$n_minus $n_plus" = "2 2" ])"
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    echo "## R6. the record pairs installed (change XLG)"
    ls "$B/records" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/records.names"
    n_rec=$(count_lines "$B/records.names")
    want_rec=$((2 * n_rerun_done + $([ "$DRY" = yes ] && echo 0 || echo 2)))
    echo "  record files written in <work>/records: $n_rec; expected $want_rec (a pair per rerun$([ "$DRY" = yes ] || echo ", and the open record's pair"))"
    check "the record files are the pairs expected" "$(yn [ "$n_rec" = "$want_rec" ])"
    no_path() { [ "$(cat "$B/records/"* | count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    check "no record file names a machine path or the corpus directory" "$(yn no_path)"
    printf 'a line naming /tmp/x\n' >"$B/c-path"
    check "control: the same form finds a planted path" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' "$B/c-path")" = 1 ])"
    if [ "$DRY" = yes ]; then
      echo "  DRY=yes: nothing installed in <repo>/records"
    else
      n_inst=0
      while IFS= read -r f; do
        if [ -e "records/$f" ]; then echo "    records/$f is already there: not installed"; continue; fi
        install -m 644 "$B/records/$f" "records/$f" || continue
        cmp -s "$B/records/$f" "records/$f" && n_inst=$((n_inst + 1))
        echo "    installed records/$f: sha256 $(sha_of "records/$f"), $(wc -c <"records/$f") bytes"
      done <"$B/records.names"
      check "every record file was installed, byte for byte" "$(yn [ "$n_inst" = "$n_rec" ])"
    fi
    
    echo
    if [ "$DRY" = yes ]; then
      echo "## the dry run's own directories removed (change XLH)"
      for d in "${DRY_RUN_DIRS[@]}" "$STAGE"; do
        echo "command: rm -rf <the directory this run made>: ${d##*/}"
        rm -rf "${d:?}"
      done
      rm -f "${ZIP:?}"
      gone_all() { local d; for d in "${DRY_RUN_DIRS[@]}" "$STAGE" "$ZIP"; do [ ! -e "$d" ] || return 1; done; }
      check "the dry run directory, the dry stage and the dry zip are gone" "$(yn gone_all)"
    fi
    
    echo
    echo "## status after the run"
    echo "command: git status --porcelain"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    st_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    echo "status lines: $st_all; of them this phase's logs, records or planning's spec: $st_ours"
    status_accounted() { [ "$st_all" != error ] && [ "$st_ours" != error ] && [ "$st_all" = "$st_ours" ]; }
    check "every change in the working tree is one of this phase's logs or records, or planning's spec" "$(yn status_accounted)"
    
    echo
    echo "## this script's own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    nerr=$(wc -c <"$ERR")
    cp "$ERR" "$B/c-err"; printf 'x' >>"$B/c-err"
    nerr_ctl=$(wc -c <"$B/c-err")
    echo "  command: wc -c <scripts>/out/run.stderr: $nerr bytes; a copy with one byte appended: $nerr_ctl"
    check "this script wrote nothing to its standard error" "$(yn [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same count reads one byte more in the copy" "$(yn [ "$nerr_ctl" = "$((nerr + 1))" ])"
    echo "run ended at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    echo "run log checks all as expected: $([ "$fail" -eq 0 ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    exec 1>&3
    wait "$SCRUB_PID"
    [ "$fail" -eq 0 ]

## the shared counting library this log sources
    # emend shared counting forms (specs/0007-gate-self-test.md, "scripts/counting.sh").
    #
    # Sourced by scripts/gate-self-test.sh and by the log scripts of later phases,
    # which use these instead of carrying their own copy.
    #
    # WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. In T3 P4 four counting sites compared a bare `grep -c`
    # with 0 without reading the exit status, so a read error printed 0 and the
    # check passed. Two independent checks found them, and the class was declared
    # closed three further times while instances still stood: a helper whose first
    # repair read grep's status while `cat` was the failing command, and both
    # halves of one function in T2 P7. Planning's remedy is that every counting
    # form, including a throwaway one, is a named function that reads the exit
    # status and has a positive control, from the start.
    #
    # Every function prints either a number or the word "error". None of them ever
    # prints a matched line, a value, or a path. A caller that compares a result
    # with 0 therefore cannot mistake a failed read for an absence.
    #
    # counting_controls runs every form against a match, a miss and an unreadable
    # file, prints one line per control, and sets counting_controls_ok. Callers run
    # it before using any form.
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    
    # count_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: total matching lines across the
    # files, or "error" if any file could not be read. The files go to grep
    # directly: with `cat file | grep -c`, an unreadable file makes CAT fail while
    # grep counts 0 over the empty stream and exits 1, so the read error reads as
    # "no hits".
    count_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_from_file <-F|-E> <pattern file> <file>...: the same, with the patterns
    # read from a file (grep -f), so a pattern is never printed.
    count_from_file() {
      local mode=$1 patterns=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -f "$patterns" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_bytes <tr class> <file>...: total bytes of that class across the files,
    # or "error" if any file could not be read. Each file is read on its own rather
    # than through `cat "$@" | tr`, for the same reason as above.
    count_bytes() {
      local class=$1 total=0 f n
      shift
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd "$class" <"$f" | wc -c) || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_lines <file>...: total lines, or "error" if any file could not be read.
    count_lines() {
      local total=0 f n
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(wc -l <"$f") || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_matches_i <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: count_matches with -i, the form
    # the hygiene step uses for OFFICE_RE and ZONE_RE. It lived in a log script as a
    # hand-rolled copy with no control of its own (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap
    # 14); a counting form belongs here, with a control, even a throwaway one.
    count_matches_i() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c -i "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # run_lines <command...>: run the command, and print the number of lines it
    # wrote on stdout, or "error" if the command itself failed. The log scripts
    # asserted a clean working tree with
    #   git status --porcelain >file 2>/dev/null || : >file
    # which turns a FAILED git status into an empty file, so the check read a
    # failed command as a clean tree (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap 1; planning
    # reproduced it). Reading the command's exit status is the whole point: a
    # command that could not run is never the same as a command that found nothing.
    run_lines() {
      local out rc
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | wc -l | tr -d ' '
    }
    
    # run_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <command...>: the same, counting only the lines
    # that match, so a caller can compare "all lines" with "lines of the expected
    # shape" without either count hiding a failed command.
    run_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" || true
    }
    
    CTRL_CLASS='\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177'
    NONASCII_CLASS='\200-\377'
    
    # counting_controls <label prefix>: run every counting form above against a
    # fixture that must match and one that must not, and against an unreadable
    # file, printing one line per result. Sets counting_controls_ok to yes or no.
    # This is the positive control planning requires for every form, and it also
    # proves each form reports "error" rather than 0 when it cannot read.
    counting_controls() {
      local d ok=yes r
      d=$(mktemp -d) || { counting_controls_ok=no; return; }
      printf 'alpha\nbeta needle gamma\nneedle\n' >"$d/hit"
      printf 'nothing of interest\n' >"$d/miss"
      printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m\017 y\ncaf\303\251\n' >"$d/bytes"
      printf 'needle\n' >"$d/patterns"
      printf 'unreadable\n' >"$d/locked"
      chmod 000 "$d/locked"
    
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit");        echo "  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/miss");       echo "  control count_matches on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_matches summed over two files: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -E 'ne+dle' "$d/hit");      echo "  control count_matches with a regular expression: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/locked");     echo "  control count_matches on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/hit"); echo "  control count_from_file on the same file: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_from_file on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_from_file on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/bytes");    echo "  control count_bytes, control bytes in a file with ESC, ESC and SI: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$d/bytes"); echo "  control count_bytes, non-ASCII bytes in a file with one two-byte character: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/miss");     echo "  control count_bytes on a clean file: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_bytes on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/hit");                    echo "  control count_lines on a three-line file: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/locked");                 echo "  control count_lines on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      printf 'NEEDLE\nneedle\n' >"$d/mixedcase"
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/mixedcase"); echo "  control count_matches_i on mixed case: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/mixedcase");  echo "  control count_matches on the same file, case sensitive: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_matches_i on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines printf 'a\nb\nc\n');            echo "  control run_lines on a command printing three lines: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines true);                          echo "  control run_lines on a command printing nothing: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines false);                         echo "  control run_lines on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines "$d/no-such-command");          echo "  control run_lines on a command that cannot run: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle printf 'needle\nother\n'); echo "  control run_matches on a command printing one match: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle false);             echo "  control run_matches on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
    
      chmod 644 "$d/locked"
      rm -rf "${d:?}"
      counting_controls_ok=$ok
      echo "  counting controls: $([ "$ok" = yes ] && echo "all as expected" || echo FAILED)"
    }

